# Cursor Rules for Grocery App

## Database Migrations

- NEVER run `npx drizzle-kit push` or `npx drizzle-kit migrate` commands
- ONLY generate migrations with `npx drizzle-kit generate`
- The app handles database migrations automatically at runtime
- When schema changes are made, generate the migration but don't apply it

## InstantDB

- This app uses InstantDB for real-time data sync
- Always use the InstantDB MCP tools to understand schema and permissions
- Schema is defined in `instant.schema.ts`, permissions in `instant.perms.ts`
- Use `@instantdb/react-native` for client-side operations
- Always pass `schema` when initializing Instant for type safety
- Use `id()` from InstantDB to generate IDs for new entities
- When transactions involve links that affect permissions, pass `ruleParams` to provide context
- For transactions that create records and link them, ensure the user has permission on BOTH the new record AND any linked records
- When linking creates reverse links, InstantDB treats it as an update to the linked entity - ensure permissions allow this
- Use InstaQL utility types (`InstaQLEntity`) for typing data models

## Code Style

- Use TypeScript strict mode
- Follow existing patterns for component structure
- Use Tailwind CSS for styling
- Prefer functional components with hooks
- Use proper TypeScript types for all props and state

## File Organization

- Keep feature-specific components in their respective feature directories
- Use shared components from `/components` directory
- Follow the existing naming conventions
- Group related functionality together

## React Native Specific

- Use React Native components and APIs
- Follow React Native best practices for performance
- Use proper navigation patterns with Expo Router
- Handle platform differences appropriately

## Testing

- Write tests for utility functions
- Test component behavior, not implementation details
- Use proper mocking for external dependencies
